==Old Tupi==

===Etymology===
From {{m|tpw|Tupi}}, a mythological figure said to be the ancestor of all Tupian peoples.<ref>{{R:tpw:Navarro 2013|+|484|1}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|tpw|/tuˈpi/}}
* {{rhyme|tpw|i|s=2}}
* {{hyph|tpw|tu|pi}}
* {{homophone|tpw|Tupi}}

===Noun===
{{tpw-noun|u}}

# [[Tupi]] {{gl|any of several related indigenous nations of coastal Brazil that spoke [[Old Tupi]]}}
#* {{quote-book|tpw|year=16th century|author=Joseph of Anchieta|title=Teatro de Anchieta|location=São Paulo|publisher=Editora Martins Fontes|year_published=1999|compiler=Maria de Lourdes de Paula Martins|translator=w:Eduardo de Almeida Navarro|page=140
|text=— Asó '''tupi''' moangaîpapa.<br>— Mba'e apŷabap'aîpó?<br>— Tupinakyîa keygûara.
|t=— I go, making the '''tupi''' sin.<br>— Which men are these?<br>—The Tupiniquim who live here.}}
# {{lb|tpw|strict}} the [[Tupian]] people that lived in the [[São Vicente]] capitancy.

